WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.900
What matters to me is your feelings as you participate in this contest... your attitude toward music.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:13.070
Which means... that I cannot accept you.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.440
It's been one week, and I haven't met Tsukimori-kun since then.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.090
Crescendo of Uneasiness

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.230
Sempai?

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.080
Shimizu-kun...

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.680
You dropped your score.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.710
Thank you.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.720
Is this the piece you are doing for the third selection?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.770
Yeah.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.330
Um, how about you, Shimizu-kun?

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.860
I was thinking of reading a book.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.080
Oh! You can sit right here.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.030
OK...

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.460
You seem kind of sleepy.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.960
I was playing the cello, and before I realized it the sun had risen.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.890
Is it OK to play at home that late?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:54.230
At night I play in a basic soundproof booth I have in my room.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.480
Don't tell me the reason you always seem tired, Shimizu-kun, is that you...

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.420
You really work hard, don't you?

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.930
Sleeping just like a baby, I see.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.470
Are your preparations for the selection going well?

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.590
You're not going to say "withdraw" like you did before, then?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.400
You want me to say that?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.900
No, I don't, it's just...

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.210
But...

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.880
I won't say it to someone who looks so down as you.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.070
Someone who looks so down...

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.730
Practice?

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.560
Yeah.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.640
Do your best.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.570
Tsuchiura!

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.630
Hihara-sempai.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.240
Are you also going to the roof?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.780
Yeah. You, too?

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.670
I was going to ask to record his playing, so I could listen and study it.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.200
I see.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.390
Hino?

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.850
Is something up, Kaho-chan?

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.830
No, it's nothing.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:02.900
I was thinking of practicing on the roof, but then I was like "maybe I should use the practice rooms after all."

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:03.940
So, bye!

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.230
Hey!

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.920
She's been acting kind of weird lately.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.700
True.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.790
I think it was right around the time we went to help out Osaki-sempai.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.970
Did something happen between her and Tsukimori-kun?

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.120
Tsukimori?

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:33.140
Hey, Tsuchiura! Where are you going all of a sudden?

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.100
What did you do to her?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.300
Her?

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.340
Hino, I mean Hino.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.230
Ever since back then, and even now...

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.250
Now?

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.630
Yeah. She just ran down the stairs with a gloomy face.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.830
She didn't come up here.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.350
Really?

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:57.330
Yeah.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.390
If you didn't do anything, then why is she acting so strange?

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.890
Why don't you ask her yourself?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:08.630
Anyway, you seem to have plenty of free time, considering the third selection is tomorrow.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:12.740
This isn't the time to be worrying about her, don't you think?

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.140
And what does what happens to her matter to you in the first place?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.980
Tsuchiura!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.190
Why?

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.190
Why do you get so worked up over Hino?

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:29.290
Damn you...

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:37.790
Perhaps the one I want to ask that is myself.  {check}

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.300
Once more from the top.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.560
I can't accept you.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.670
I started to rain so suddenly.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.540
Wait, Kahoko, you're sopping wet!

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.750
I'm sorry, did you get wet?

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.860
I... love this violin.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:33.310
Before I realized it, I've fallen in love.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:40.120
I love this violin! Right now, it's all I have...

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.520
It's already the third time.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.560
Tsukimori-kun...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.710
G-Good morning.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.160
Good morning.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.870
I love the violin.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:13.240
That's why I'm going to perform with all my heart today.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.350
Ah, your dress is so cute, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.550
U-Um...

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.570
It looks good on you, Shoko-chan!

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.410
Don't you think, Hino-san?

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.800
Right, sure. You're always wearing such cute clothes, Fuyuumi-chan.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.680
They're not really...

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.000
That sure is nice. Something like that doesn't look good on me, though.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.130
I wish the accompanists could dress up, too.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.170
No kidding, Mori-sempai!

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:51.880
My, oh, my, it sure is lively in the room next door.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.940
It sure is.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.130
So, everyone.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.680
It's tied with a granny knot, Shimizu-kun.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:13.940
Granny?

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:21.040
That's right, Tsuchiura-kun. Lately Hino-san has seemed kind of down. Did something happen with her?

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.250
I don't anything about it.  Nothing to do with me.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.710
OK, finished.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.800
Thank you very much.

00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:42.190
Everyone, after you are ready, it's about time to get started.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.610
Osaki-sempai, why are you here?

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:51.310
I always come to listen to the selections, but today I'm helping out Kanazawa-sensei.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:54.240
I see. Thanks for helping out.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.040
It's not a problem at all.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.880
Did something happen? Everyone's acting a bit weird.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.570
No clue.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.670
Time sure flies. It's already the third time, you know?

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:33.070
We will now begin the third selection of Seiso Academy's School-wide Competition.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:45.250
Doesn't the crowd seem a bit more excited than last time?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:51.080
You all seem to have gotten used to this by now and are enjoying yourselves.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:55.420
During the first selection, you guys from General Studies were totally shell-shocked, you know?

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:58.140
Oh, I see.

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:03.440
That's true. I didn't really listen to everyone's performance.

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:05.970
Today, I'm going to listen carefully.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:12.510
Performer 1, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.650
Hihara-kun, good luck.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.820
He will be playing Schubert's Serenade.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.440
Hihara-sempai?

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.090
What?

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:23.820
Don't you think he's acting a little strange?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:47.530
He seems to have started off well enough.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.390
Another?

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.600
Hihara-sempai missed a lot of notes.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.080
I wonder what's wrong?

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.480
Hihara-kun, what's the matter? Are you OK?

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.590
Yeah, I just wasn't feeling it.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.680
That sucked.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:16.440
Performer 2, from the Music Department, class 1-A, Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:19.260
He will be playing Siciliene, by Fauré.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.740
Shimizu-kun is calm?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.910
Ah, what a nice sound!

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:47.390
No, it's that his performances are always so serious and faithful to the score.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:51.350
But today, he's straying a little bit.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:52.310
Yeah.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.170
He's uneasy.

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.520
Shimizu-kun.

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.410
You'll be fine.

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:18.590
But...

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:22.130
It's only natural to be nervous, right?

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:28.090
Performer 3, from the Music Department, class 1-B, Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:32.850
She will be playing the second movement of Three Romances, by Schumann.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.830
Fuyuumi-chan, you can do it!

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:38.460
We'll be cheering for you from over here!

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:39.960
Sempai...

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.510
Fuyuumi-chan, good luck!

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:44.150
Kaho-sempai...

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:46.400
I'll do my best!

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:55.870
Oh, Fuyuumi... Her performance level among the clarinet majors is considerable, but...

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:01.540
It can't be helped, she's just too introverted.

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:07.550
But because she's that kind of person, don't you think this competition will be good experience for her?

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:15.720
I want to play just like Kaho-sempai's carefree performance.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:32.100
Huh? She's really good today.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:34.830
This piece really shows off her talents.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:46.500
It's such a pretty sound. People who've been playing since they were little are just in another league.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.230
She's really calm today.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:30.030
Good job!

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.690
Good for you, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.830
Yeah! You sounded great!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.040
It was a wonderful performance.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:37.560
Thank you very much.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:44.350
I said we should do our best together, so since Fuyuumi-chan did her part...

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.320
But, I'm...

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:52.510
Performer 4, from the Music Department, class 2-A, Len Tsukimori-kun.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.990
He will be playing Tzigane, by Ravel.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:17:00.120
Tsukimori withdrew last time, I suppose there's no way he could win.

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:35.860
That's a high level of excellence.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.330
That's very nice, Tsukimori-sempai.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:05.680
What am I going to do? He's on an entirely different level!

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:11.970
How am I supposed to go after an amazing performance like that?

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:31.390
What's with you, Tsukimori? Why the "man, what a pain" face?

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:33.840
I thought it was quite excellent.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.760
Yeah, well...

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:42.100
It's just that, I was thinking if I had time to practice a bit more, I could have...

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:48.590
Performer 5, from General Studies, class 2-5, Ryotaro Tsuchiura.

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:51.150
He will be playing Revolution, by Chopin.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.610
Tsuchiura, good luck!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.860
Wow! You go, Tsuchiura!

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:41.140
Tsuchiura-kun is amazing, too. What am I going to do? How can I perform on the same stage as these people?

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:55.460
"I love the violin." That's just naive!

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:59.220
I'll never be able to catch up to them with just that!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.860
Tsuchiura, amazing!

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:19.190
Hino?

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:26.870
Performer 6, from General Studies, class 2-2, Kahoko Hino-san.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.670
She will be playing Melodie, by Tchaikovsky.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:32.770
Hino-san.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:18.840
It's no good, at this rate...

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.400
Magical violin, I beg of you!

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:27.180
Let me play more beautifully, more accurately, so I can catch up to everyone else!

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:30.480
What's wrong, Kahoko Hino?

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:37.650
Ring higher!

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.610
You can't!

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:40.230
Play stronger!

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:43.950
You can't place those kinds of feelings on the violin!

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:47.860
Please, Magical violin, sing for me!

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.660
More, more!

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:44.260
Unexpected things can happen on the stage sometimes.

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:51.190
For example, there was once a conductor who was jumping around so vigorously that he fell off the stage,

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:55.290
but he got back up immediately and continued to conduct as if nothing had happened.

00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:58.380
Well, no one knows if it's really true or not.

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.270
OK, now time for a quiz!

00:24:00.270 --> 00:24:05.130
If the soloist breaks a string, how do they continue the performance?

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:10.340
What? Hino doesn't feel like doing the preview today?

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:13.890
What are we going to do with her? I'll do it in her place.

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:17.680
Next episode: Partita of Grief.

00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:20.100
Be quiet and listen to my flute.

00:24:20.410 --> 00:24:24.330
The answer is... She borrows the concert master's violin!
